// latchfixb (2026-10-12), found by the review of crawlerlatch, a BALANCE fix: an ELITE that hangs on keeps its harder bite
// (13 x 1.6 = 20.8) but bites on a clock 1.6 times slower, so a latched elite hurts at the rate a latched normal one does.
// Measured before this: one latched elite downed a full-health man with no armour in 2.8 s (bites at 0, 0.7 ... 2.8),
// walking, sprinting or rolling alike, because nothing shakes a latched crawler off now; a normal one takes 4.9 s. Before
// the latch only a man standing still took that rate; anyone moving outwalked it. Now about 4.5 s, and its 2.2 times the
// health is still what makes it the dangerous one: it stays on you longer while you kill it.
if(e.cd<=0){ LATCH_BITE=1; try{ netHitPlayer(_lb,e.dmg*(e.elite?(CFG.eliteDmg===undefined?1.6:CFG.eliteDmg):1),'crawler',e.name,e.x,e.y); } finally{ LATCH_BITE=0; } e.cd=.7*(e.elite?Math.max(1,(CFG.eliteDmg===undefined?1.6:CFG.eliteDmg)):1); }

